        <type>BPCODEC_EXPORT bool</type>
        <definition>bool Bpv6Fragmenter::Fragment</definition>
        <argsstring>(BundleViewV6 &amp;orig, uint64_t sz, std::list&lt; BundleViewV6 &gt; &amp;fragments)</argsstring>
        <name>Fragment</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classBundleViewV6" kindref="compound">BundleViewV6</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>orig</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint64_t</type>
          <declname>sz</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>std::list&lt; <ref refid="classBundleViewV6" kindref="compound">BundleViewV6</ref> &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>fragments</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Fragment bundle into multiple fragments of size sz per RFC5050</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>orig</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The bundle to fragment </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sz</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The max payload size for each fragmetn </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fragments[out]</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The fragments if successful</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true if able to fragment, false otherwise</para>
</simplesect>
The original bundle is not modified. sz must be greater than zero and smaller than the length of the payload of the original bundle.</para>
<para>The payload of the fragmented bundles will be at most sz bytes long. Upon successful fragmentation, there will be at least two fragments. All fragments will have payloads of size sz except for possibly the last fragment.</para>
<para>The original bundle must not be dirty. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
